ing the final plays\n\nMy teammate might have a 2 or joker. Even if they don\'t and the Landlord takes control, I still have my ♦2 and ♦A as strong cards for later critical moments.\n\nReason:\n\nI should **pass** to preserve my ♦2. This is early game with all players holding 14-15 cards. Using the second-highest ranked card in the game (2) to beat a single Ace is strategically poor. The 2 has much more value in the endgame when it can prevent the Landlord from winning or help secure victory. My teammate may also have high cards to play. Even if the Landlord gains control now, preserving premium cards for critical moments is the correct long-term strategy.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
